<title>Acute Sialadenitis: Management</title>
<graphic href="eee0114-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient with unilateral swelling and tenderness of a salivary gland. Systemic symptoms (fever, chills) or area of fluctuance over gland? </label>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Begin broad-spectrum antibiotic; consider heat, massage, sialogogues.</label>
<path target="cell-4"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Patient improved?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-6">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Continue treatment until symptoms resolve.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Obtain ultrasound or CT and treat based on findings (ie, abscess, tumor). Consider sialendoscopy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Obtain needle aspirate; admit for parenteral antibiotics and surgical consultation</label>
<path target="cell-7"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Abscess diagnosed?</label>
<path target="cell-6">No</path>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Surgical drainage.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
